 pretty keen on my crackpot constellation  thoughts no matter what it turns out to  be though i'm curious as to how hoshi  actually marked megami because he wasn't  touched in any way like divine dog  appears to have been what's also very  curious is that akutami takes some very  specific space to show the dropping of a  phone and it's quite unclear exactly  what happened here because hoshi takes  the phone out holds it in left hand but  then divine dog strikes the phone is  nowhere to be seen but then we see both  the phone and divine dog repelled and  i'm probably just reading too much into  this because that's the thing that i do  but it does make me wonder if the phone  might have been marked with a star as  well and it's forming part of the  technique here either that or akatami is  just making a point of having hershey  drop the phone to emphasize that we can  now no longer contact hakari sometimes  things don't need to be quite as  complicated as i may make them out to be  i just find it very interesting because  drawing manga is an  extraordinarily time time-consuming  process and artists learn very quickly  not to draw superfluous stuff so when i  see a panel like this i just ask myself  alright so what was their intention here  because potentially hours of work went  into this singular panel so akutami must  have thought it to be very important  either in a technical sense of ability  or for the sake of narrative now of  course something i haven't mentioned yet  is the gender reveal of hoshi kirara we  do take some time out of this chapter to  quite blatantly state that hoshi is male  at least biologically i suppose and i  think the question does come up here  because kirara is actually a very  classically female name like not in the  way that hoshi kirar's name is composed  because that's a very strange cobbling  together of kanji but the more common  kanji combination for kirara contains  the symbols for both cloud and mother  which is why i think megami twigs here  because he hears the name kirara and  he's all like kirara i thought that the  other third year was a male student  which to put into an english context i  don't know suppose imagine hearing a  name like say stephanie and then being  told that stephanie is a man that's what  i think is happening with megami here  the gender expectations being flipped on  him which is actually quite ironic  coming from one megumi fushiguro whose  first name is also classically  attributed to being female so this does  seem to be perhaps an emerging motif  with akutami purposely subverting gender  expectations and hey in a very rare  instance for shona manga we might  actually have a legit lgbt relationship  happening with hoshi and hakari which i  do think is worth pointing out if that  is indeed the case because yeah it's far  from a first for shona manga but it  generally wouldn't be shown so  explicitly they'd usually be buried  behind a mountain of subtext meanwhile i  think my genuine highlight of this  chapter is this nice sliver of darkness  actually my favorite panel by far has to  be this shot of megami emerging from the  shadow of some dude but it's  terrifyingly cool almost like a shark  skillfully and patiently hunting its  prey below the deep dark waters i say  this a lot about megami but i swear he  just continues to get better and better  with every passing off because he just  keeps diversifying his skill set and  being generally awesome he's one of the  many characters who could take the  mantle of protagonist in the event that  yuji was magically erased from the  series somehow because i for one would  quite happily follow the tale of megumi  fushiguru still curious as to how he's  going to react to this whole zenin  clan's slaughter business because unless  i've missed something i'm assuming that  this hakari recruitment business is  happening in tandem with maki's quest  for very specific blood and just while  we're on that actually a couple of  peopl